11         
12             Using this program:
13         
14               * See USER PROCESSING AND SETTINGS, below, to configure this program for your environment and data
15               * Program will plot all studies, ordered by STUDYID, with maximum of 20 boxes on a page (default)
16                 + see user option MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE, below, to change limit of 20 boxes per page
17               * Program separately plots all parameters provided in PARAMCD
18               * Measurements within each PARAMCD and ATPTN determine precision of statistical results
19                 + MEAN gets 1 extra decimal, STD DEV gets 2 extra decimals
20                 + see macro UTIL_VALUE_FORMAT to modify this behavior
21               * If your treatment names are too long for the summary table, abbreviate them
22                 in the input data, and add a footnote that explains your short Tx codes
23                 + This program contains custom code to shorted Tx labels in the PhUSE CS test data
24                 + See "2b) USER SUBSET of data", below
25         
26             NOTES:
27               Design decision:
28                 * User must specify a baseline visit number, and a post-baseline visit number.
29                 * An alternative approach: User specifies an analysis flag that identifies exactly 1
30                   post-baseline obs per subject (per param, analysis timepoint), and a BASELINE var that contains
31                   the corresponding baseline. See for example WPCT-F.07.07.sas, which uses this approach.
