                                                           The SAS System

54         
55             1) REQUIRED - PhUSE CS Utilities macro library.
56                These templates require the PhUSE CS macro utilities:
57                  https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/utilities
58                User must ensure that SAS can find PhUSE CS macros in the SASAUTOS path (see EXECUTE ONE TIME, below)
59         
60             2) OPTIONAL - Subset measurement data, to limit resulting plots to specific
61                  - Parameters
62                  - Analysis Timepoints
63                  - Visits
64         
65             3) REQUIRED - Key user settings (libraries, data sets, variables and box plot options)
66                M_LB:   Libname containing ADaM measurement data, such as ADVS.
67                        WORK by default, since step (2) creates the desired WORK subset.
68                M_DS:   Measuments data set, such as ADVS.
69         
70                T_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Name, such as TRTP, TRTA.
71                TN_VAR: Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Number (display controls order), such as TRTPN, TRTAN.
72                M_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with measurements data, such as AVAL.
73                LO_VAR: Variable in M_DS with LOWER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRLO.
74                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
75                HI_VAR: Variable in M_DS with UPPER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRHI.
76                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
77         
78                P_FL:  Population flag variable. 'Y' indicates record is in population of interest.
79                A_FL:  Analysis Flag variable.   'Y' indicates BASELINE and POST-BASELINE obs that contain:
80                         * A non-missing measurement             (either LAST, MIN or MAX for the timepoint AVISITN)
81                         * including a non-missing baseline      (LAST, MIN or MAX to match the measurement)
82                         * and a non-missing chg from baseline   (based on the above baseline & post-baseline measurements)
83                   NB: Exactly 1 BL and 1 PBL measure for each STUDYID, TRTPN, USUBJID, PARAMCD, ATPTN.
84                   NB: AVISITN identifies Baseline (lesser value) from Post-baseline (greater values) measure.
85                       For an example, see the PhUSE CS derivation in ADaM/derive_lastminmax_measure.sas
86         
87                C_MODE: Change Mode label. This is merely a label that describes the obs flagged by user-specified A_FL
88                         * LAST: Default. Change from LAST baseline to LAST post-baseline analysis measurement
89                         * MIN:  Change from MIN baseline to MIN post-baseline analysis measurement
90                         * MAX:  Change from MAX baseline to MAX post-baseline analysis measurement
91         
92                REF_LINES:
93                      Option to specify which Normal Range reference lines to include in box plots
94                      <NONE | UNIFORM | NARROW | ALL | numeric-value(s)> See discussion in Central Tendency White Paper
95                      NONE    - No reference lines on box plot
96                      UNIFORM - Preferred alternative to default. Only plot LOW/HIGH ref lines if they are uniform for all
96       ! measurements
97                      NARROW  - Default. Display only the narrow normal limits: max LOW, and min HIGH limits
98                      ALL     - Discouraged, since displaying ALL reference lines confuses review of data display
99                      numeric-values - space-delimited list of reference line values, such as a 0 reference line for displays of
99       ! change.
100        
101               MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE:
102                     Maximum number of boxes to display per plot page (see "Notes", above)
103        
104               OUTPUTS_FOLDER:
105                     Location to write PDF outputs (WITHOUT final back- or forward-slash)
106        
